# Trivy ignore file for the M10 CI pipeline.
#
# Only add an entry here for a finding that has been explicitly reviewed
# and documented (see PROJECT_SCOPE.md M9 severity policy). Do not add
# blanket ignores. Each entry below must reference the specific
# vulnerability ID and explain why it is excepted.

# CVE-2026-59873 (CRITICAL) - tar, "Denial of Service via crafted gzip bomb".
# Reviewed in M9 and confirmed again while building M10's CI pipeline
# locally: this is inside npm's own bundled tooling
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/...) baked into the node:22-alpine base
# image, not a dependency of this application (app/node_modules contains
# 0 vulnerabilities per the same scan - only "express" and its own small
# transitive tree). The app never invokes npm's bundled tar. Fix is
# upstream (a newer node:22-alpine release); nothing in this repo's code,
# Dockerfiles, or dependencies can remediate it directly. Remove this
# line once the base image ships a patched npm/tar.
CVE-2026-59873

